new-player-guide-page-welcome-title = Welcome to Reserve Station!
new-player-guide-page-welcome-text =
    Before you read the server rules, let's quickly set the game up for you. It takes less than a minute.

    All of these settings can be changed later in the "Options" menu (Esc). The server rules will be shown once you are done.

new-player-guide-page-speech-title = Speech style above the head
new-player-guide-page-speech-text =
    Character speech above their heads can be shown either as compact Runechat text or as classic speech bubbles.

    Pick whichever you prefer. You can always change it in the "Options" menu (Esc).
new-player-guide-speech-runechat = Runechat style
new-player-guide-speech-runechat-desc = Compact coloured pixel text above the speaker.
new-player-guide-speech-bubbles = Speech bubbles
new-player-guide-speech-bubbles-desc = Classic dialogue bubbles popping up above the character.
new-player-guide-speech-bubbles-names = Show names
new-player-guide-speech-bubbles-background = Show name background
new-player-guide-speech-preview-title = This is what it looks like:

new-player-guide-page-hud-title = HUD layout
new-player-guide-page-hud-text =
    The standard HUD puts the chat and the panels on top of the game field. The separated HUD moves the chat into its own column on the right: the chat no longer covers the game field, but the field itself becomes narrower.

    Pick whichever is comfortable. You can switch at any time.
new-player-guide-hud-standard-desc = Chat in the top-right corner, more room for the game field, and it is what the Roblox kids are used to.
new-player-guide-hud-separated-desc = Chat in a separate column on the right with extra features, handy for reading through dialogue and small interactions, the classic SS13 interface.

new-player-guide-page-mood-title = Mood effects
new-player-guide-page-mood-text =
    On this build your character has a mood that changes with what happens around them: good food and drinks bring joy, while injuries, handcuffs and stress make it worse.

    Mood directly affects your character's physical state and how they perceive the world. Below you can set up the mood visual effects (the same option can be found in the "Options" -> "Graphics" menu).
new-player-guide-mood-enabled = Enable effects
new-player-guide-mood-disabled = Disable effects
new-player-guide-mood-enabled-desc = The screen becomes brighter and more vivid when happy, and fades towards black and white under stress and depression.
new-player-guide-mood-disabled-desc = The game's colours always stay the same.
new-player-guide-mood-info-title = How mood affects the game:
new-player-guide-mood-info-speed-title = Speed bonus and penalty
new-player-guide-mood-info-speed-desc = A happy character moves noticeably faster, while a depressed one slows down.
new-player-guide-mood-info-visual-title = Overlay
new-player-guide-mood-info-visual-desc = A screen shader smoothly changes the world's colour saturation depending on your character's emotional state.
new-player-guide-mood-info-alert-title = Seeing the reasons
new-player-guide-mood-info-alert-desc = Click the mood icon in the right alert panel to see the full list of emotional factors affecting your character in chat.
